In 4.6, setters and getters already perform serialization assuming the `libraries/xxxxx` path.

As compatibility code, the setter is written to parse dictionaries passed with the `libraries` path. However, enabling the getter to retrieve dictionaries with the `libraries` path, as shown below, does not resolve this issue.

```cpp
bool AnimationMixer::_get(const StringName &p_name, Variant &r_ret) const {
	String name = p_name;

#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED
#ifdef TOOLS_ENABLED
	if (name == "libraries") {
		r_ret = get_animation_libraries();
	} else if (name.begins_with("libraries/")) {
#endif // TOOLS_ENABLED
#else
	if (name.begins_with("libraries/")) {
#endif // DISABLE_DEPRECATED
		String which = name.get_slicec('/', 1);
		if (has_animation_library(which)) {
			r_ret = get_animation_library(which);
		} else {
			return false;
		}
	} else {
		return false;
	}

	return true;
}

#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED
