However, my change adds `EXTRACT_PARAM_OR_FAIL_V(..., ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER)` on top, meaning `ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER` is returned. In my opinion this is the more "canonical" error being returned for incorrectly using a null parameter.

